# Black Duo: a second pan on the seven middle black keys, in a scale that goes with the first
# (params: 24 Scale 25 Key 26 Black 27 Duo 28 Duo level; duoI: the second pan's note I, 0 its ding)
wait 1600
tap SEL
expect view 7
# off (Kit): the Duo page's Duo knobs do nothing
tap SEL
expect view 8
spin K1 1
expect par27 0
wait 50
shot duo_off.png
tap SEL
spin K4 1
expect par26 1
wait 50
shot duo_keys.png
# D Kurd's best match: D Celtic, its ding an octave over the first's
expect duocount >3
expect duo0 6200
expect duo1 6900
expect duo2 7200
# the end keys stay the steel
key b0 down
wait 20
expect shellL >5
key b0 up
# the middle keys play the second pan, laid out as the white keys are: Pan, its ding in the middle
# (b5), its fields alternating outward, left first: D Celtic D4 | A4 C5 D5 E5 F5 G5
expect duokey5 6200
expect duokey4 6900
expect duokey6 7200
expect duokey3 7400
expect duokey7 7600
expect duokey2 7700
expect duokey8 7900
expect duokey1 -1
tapkey b5
wait 30
expect note6200 >3
tapkey b6
wait 30
expect note7200 >3
wait 50
shot duo_play.png
# Mirror: right first; Linear: low to high, the ding on the left
expect view 7
spin K1 1
expect par23 1
expect duokey5 6200
expect duokey6 6900
expect duokey4 7200
expect duokey2 7900
spin K1 1
expect par23 2
expect duokey2 6200
expect duokey5 7400
expect duokey8 7900
spin K1 -2
expect par23 0
# Duo level 0: the second pan barely there
tap SEL
expect view 8
spin K2 -80
expect par28 0
tapkey b4
wait 30
expect note6900 <15
spin K2 80
expect par28 80
tap SEL
expect view 7
# another match: the Duo page's first knob steps through them, each in the first pan's notes
tap SEL
expect view 8
spin K1 1
expect par27 1
wait 50
shot duo_next.png
spin K1 40
expect par27 >1
spin K1 -60
expect par27 0
# a new scale (or key) starts the match afresh
spin K1 2
expect par27 2
tap SEL
spin K2 1
expect par24 1
expect par27 0
turn PRESET 1
expect par27 0
expect dropped 0
